schema_version: 1

# Draft curator-facing model catalog input.
#
# Purpose:
# - Keep this file human-writable.
# - Fill in only the labels you can actually read from the CLI or UI.
# - Do not translate values into runtime/internal forms.
#
# Runtime normalization is intentionally a later cats-runtime responsibility.
# Inheritance rules:
# - model with no `options` key inherits shared_options in scope
# - use `options: []` to say a model has no options
# - provider shared_options override same-named catalog shared_options
#
# Provenance is per-catalog and no longer uniform - read each entry's `notes`.
# Every catalog carries a `version` and `last_updated`; `last_updated` records
# when the model list itself was last re-read or otherwise verified. A newer CLI
# version probe alone does not advance that date; its observation date and scope
# belong in `notes` until the model list can also be re-verified.
#
# Seed data was originally backfilled from local CLI versions observed on
# 2026-04-08 plus the then-current cats-runtime static/advanced baselines.
#
# 2026-08-26 refresh: Antigravity, Codex, and Cursor are account-resolved live
# CLI enumerations (`agy models`, `codex debug models`, `cursor-agent models`).
# 2026-09-02: the Claude and Codex entries were re-read from their interactive
# `/model` pickers and now carry mixed provenance - see each entry's `notes`.
# 2026-09-03: the Antigravity entry was refreshed from `agy models` on 1.1.24
# corroborated by that build's `/model` picker, and a Grok entry was added for
# the first time from the Grok CLI 1.0.13 account-resolved model manifest.
# 2026-09-05: a Muse entry was added for the first time from muse 1.0.3's own
# `model/list` reply over `muse serve`.
# 2026-09-16: Antigravity 1.2.3 picker families and effort controls refreshed;
# execution ids retain the independent 1.1.24 enumeration provenance.
# Every other entry keeps the provenance and date recorded in its own `notes`.
# Copilot, Kilo, Kiro, and Junie had their versions re-probed but not their model
# lists - those CLIs either gate the list behind an account, expose it only in an
# interactive picker, or publish a different artifact than the picker shows.
#
# Treat this file as a starting point to correct, trim, or expand.

catalogs:
  - cli: Claude
    version: 2.1.273
    last_updated: 2026-09-16
    notes:
      - "Model list and every model's effort screen re-read 2026-09-16 from the operator-pasted `/model` picker on Claude Code 2.1.273. The operator requested exactly four Cats model rows, with the duplicate Default/Opus presentation collapsed to Opus. Scope is the operator's account; entitlement elsewhere is unverified."
      - "Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/claude-2.1.273/model-picker.success.redacted.txt"
      - "The five source rows are Default (recommended), Opus (1M context), Fable, Sonnet, and Haiku. Default is a provider-default sentinel, not an executable model id. Its row and effort branch remain in evidence; Cats exposes only the four explicit model aliases, with Opus selected by default as the operator requested. This does not claim a provider-default alias will always resolve to Opus."
      - "Display names follow the operator's version-bearing projection of the picker descriptions: Opus 5 with 1M context, Fable 5.1, Sonnet 5, and Haiku 4.5. Cats adds the status suffix ` (default)` in lowercase across model and effort menus; it is not part of the model name."
      - "Raw alias mappings are unchanged: `opus`, `sonnet`, and `haiku` retain their 2.1.246 static-extraction provenance; `fable` and `claude-fable-5-1` retain the 2.1.258 help/static-artifact evidence. The existing Claude normalizers map these labels and all six effort values. No raw token is inferred from the new paste."
      - "For Default, Opus, Fable, and Sonnet separately, the complete ordered effort set is Low, Medium, High, xHigh, Max, Ultracode, with High explicitly marked `(default)`. Haiku displays `Effort not supported for Haiku` and keeps `options: []`. The Max usage warning is retained per model."
      - "Older effort descriptions remain with their earlier provenance; they were not re-observed in 2.1.273. In particular, the 2.1.258 static artifact maps Ultracode to `ultracode` and describes xHigh effort plus dynamic workflow orchestration; the earlier read-only `claude --effort ultracode --version` parser check accepted that token. This refresh does not repeat execution probes."
      - "Opus 1M context was re-observed. Sonnet 1M and Haiku 200K context values remain from the 2.1.246 static extraction and were not re-observed; Fable context remains unknown and omitted."
    models:
      - name: Opus
        label: Opus 5 with 1M context
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Opus 5 with 1M context - best for everyday, complex tasks"
        default: true
        context: 1000000
        options:
          - name: Effort
            values:
              - name: Low
                notes:
                  - "Quick, straightforward implementation with minimal overhead"
              - name: Medium
                notes:
                  - "Balanced approach with standard implementation and testing"
              - name: High
                notes:
                  - "Comprehensive implementation with extensive testing and documentation"
              - name: xHigh
                notes:
                  - "Deeper reasoning than high, just below maximum (Fable 5, Opus 4.7+, Sonnet 5)"
              - name: Max
                notes:
                  - "Maximum capability with deepest reasoning. May use excessive tokens resulting in long response times or overthinking. Use sparingly for the hardest tasks."
              - name: Ultracode
                notes:
                  - "2.1.258 static artifact description: xHigh effort plus dynamic workflow orchestration for this session only"
            default: High

      - name: Fable
        label: Fable 5.1
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Fable 5.1 - most capable for your hardest and longest-running tasks"
        options:
          - name: Effort
            values:
              - Low
              - Medium
              - High
              - xHigh
              - name: Max
                notes:
                  - "May use excessive tokens resulting in long response times or overthinking. Use sparingly for the hardest tasks."
              - name: Ultracode
                notes:
                  - "2.1.258 static artifact description: xHigh effort plus dynamic workflow orchestration for this session only"
            default: High

      - name: Sonnet
        label: Sonnet 5
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Sonnet 5 - efficient for routine tasks"
        context: 1000000
        options:
          - name: Effort
            values:
              - Low
              - Medium
              - High
              - xHigh
              - name: Max
                notes:
                  - "May use excessive tokens resulting in long response times or overthinking. Use sparingly for the hardest tasks."
              - name: Ultracode
                notes:
                  - "2.1.258 static artifact description: xHigh effort plus dynamic workflow orchestration for this session only"
            default: High

      - name: Haiku
        label: Haiku 4.5
        notes:
          - "Picker description: Haiku 4.5 - fastest for quick answers"
        context: 200000
        options: []

  - cli: Codex
    version: 0.154.0
    last_updated: 2026-09-16
    notes:
      - "Model list and all per-model reasoning screens re-read 2026-09-16 from the operator-pasted `/model` picker on Codex CLI 0.154.0. The operator confirmed the five visible rows are complete and authorized removing gpt-5.4, gpt-5.4-mini, and gpt-5.3-codex-spark from the Cats picker. Scope is the operator's account; entitlement elsewhere is unverified."
      - "Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/codex-0.154.0/model-picker.success.redacted.txt"
      - "The model ids, ordering, descriptions, reasoning sets, and defaults below were observed in that paste. gpt-6-astra is explicitly `(default)`; gpt-5.5 is only `(current)`, a session selection. This supersedes the older gpt-5.6-sol model default."
      - "Display names preserve the raw ids and casing shown by the 0.154.0 picker, as requested by the operator; older GPT-style label overrides are removed. The four retained context values come from `codex debug models` on 0.149.1 (2026-08-26) and were not re-observed. gpt-6-astra has no inferred context limit."
      - "The picker says legacy models remain accessible through `codex -m <model_name>` or config.toml. Removal from this visible catalog does not claim those ids are invalid for manual use."
      - "Context values reflect the Codex CLI catalog and may differ from OpenAI API limits"
      - "All four `More reasoning…` submenus were opened: gpt-6-astra, gpt-5.6-sol, and gpt-5.6-terra offer Max and Ultra; gpt-5.6-luna offers Max only; gpt-5.5 stops at Extra high. The Advanced Reasoning screen warns `⚠ Consumes usage limits faster`. The operator explicitly authorized a flat Cats reasoning list; navigation/grouping and usage warnings remain in the evidence."
      - "Level descriptions are identical across every captured model offering that level, so they are shared below; value availability and defaults remain model-specific. Extra high maps to xhigh through the existing Codex effort normalizer, and Max/Ultra map to max/ultra."
    shared_options:
      - name: Reasoning Level
        values:
          - name: Low
            notes:
              - "Fast responses with lighter reasoning"
          - name: Medium
            notes:
              - "Balances speed and reasoning depth for everyday tasks"
          - name: High
            notes:
              - "Greater reasoning depth for complex problems"
          - name: Extra high
            notes:
              - "Extra high reasoning depth for complex problems"
          - name: Max
            notes:
              - "For difficult problems when quality matters more than speed · higher usage"
          - name: Ultra
            notes:
              - "For demanding work using multiple agents · highest usage"
        default: Medium
    models:
      - name: gpt-6-astra
        notes:
          - "Our most capable model for complex, demanding work."
        default: true

      - name: gpt-5.6-sol
        notes:
          - "Reliable agentic workhorse for everyday tasks."
        context: 272000
        options:
          - name: Reasoning Level
            default: Low

      - name: gpt-5.6-terra
        notes:
          - "Balanced agentic coding model for everyday work."
        context: 272000

      - name: gpt-5.6-luna
        notes:
          - "Fast and affordable agentic coding model."
        context: 272000
        options:
          - name: Reasoning Level
            values: [Low, Medium, High, Extra high, Max]
            default: Medium

      - name: gpt-5.5
        notes:
          - "Proven previous-generation model for coding and general work."
        context: 272000
        options:
          - name: Reasoning Level
            values: [Low, Medium, High, Extra high]
            default: Medium

  - cli: Antigravity
    version: 1.2.3
    last_updated: 2026-09-16
    notes:
      - "Complete operator-supplied /model picker and all per-model effort screens on Antigravity CLI 1.2.3, observed 2026-09-16; account scope is the operator's CLI."
      - "Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/antigravity-1.2.3/model-picker.success.redacted.txt"
      - "Raw execution ids retain the 2026-09-03 agy models capture on 1.1.24: docs/research/fixtures/antigravity-1.1.24/models-command.success.redacted.txt. They were not re-enumerated on 1.2.3."
      - "One row per picker family. The first effort's verified raw id identifies each Gemini row; Runtime resolves model plus effort to the corresponding verified --model id. All fourteen executable choices remain represented."
      - "No model or effort is marked default. Cats initializes to the first model and first applicable effort without adding a default label; existing explicit choices are preserved."
    models:
      - name: gemini-3.8-flash-low
        label: Gemini 3.8 Flash
        options:
          - name: Effort
            values:
              - name: low
                notes: ["Faster responses, lighter reasoning — great for simpler tasks"]
              - name: medium
                notes: ["Balanced speed and reasoning quality for most tasks"]
              - name: high
                notes: ["Deepest reasoning for complex problems — slower but strongest"]
      - name: gemini-3.7-flash-low
        label: Gemini 3.7 Flash
        options:
          - name: Effort
            values:
              - name: low
                notes: ["Faster responses, lighter reasoning — great for simpler tasks"]
              - name: medium
                notes: ["Balanced speed and reasoning quality for most tasks"]
              - name: high
                notes: ["Deepest reasoning for complex problems — slower but strongest"]
      - name: gemini-3.6-flash-low
        label: Gemini 3.6 Flash
        options:
          - name: Effort
            values:
              - name: low
                notes: ["Faster responses, lighter reasoning — great for simpler tasks"]
              - name: medium
                notes: ["Balanced speed and reasoning quality for most tasks"]
              - name: high
                notes: ["Deepest reasoning for complex problems — slower but strongest"]
      - name: gemini-3.1-pro-low
        label: Gemini 3.1 Pro
        options:
          - name: Effort
            values:
              - name: low
                notes: ["Faster responses, lighter reasoning — great for simpler tasks"]
              - name: high
                notes: ["Deepest reasoning for complex problems — slower but strongest"]
      - name: claude-sonnet-4-6
        label: Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Thinking)
        options: []
      - name: claude-opus-4-6-thinking
        label: Claude Opus 4.6 (Thinking)
        options: []
      - name: gpt-oss-120b-medium
        label: GPT-OSS 120B (Medium)
        options: []

  - cli: Grok
    version: 1.0.34
    last_updated: 2026-09-17
    notes:
      - "Complete two-model /model list and per-model effort menus supplied 2026-09-17 for Grok Build 1.0.34 as operator transcription and screenshots (the TUI cannot copy text). Evidence: docs/research/fixtures/grok-1.0.34/model-picker.success.redacted.txt and effort-grok-4.6.redacted.png / effort-grok-4.5.redacted.png in the same directory."
      - "The operator confirmed the repeated Grok 4.6 heading on the three-effort screen meant Grok 4.5. Preserve picker order and visible spelling; omit the session-only (active) marker from labels."
      - "No model or effort default is declared by the supplied picker. Per explicit operator policy, Cats initializes each menu from its first applicable item without marking any item default. This supersedes the earlier curated High effort defaults from the 1.0.13 manifest; it does not claim the upstream manifest defaults changed."
      - "Raw model ids and effort label-to-token mappings are retained from the 2026-09-03 Grok 1.0.13 manifest: docs/research/fixtures/grok-1.0.13/models-cache.success.redacted.txt. The existing normalizer maps Extra High Effort / High Effort / Medium Effort / Low Effort to xhigh / high / medium / low for --reasoning-effort; the mapping was not re-enumerated on 1.0.34."
      - "Per-model descriptions from both screenshots remain in option notes, including Higher (Grok 4.6) versus Highest (Grok 4.5) for High Effort. Context 500000 is retained from the 1.0.13 manifest; no context or output limit was re-observed in this picker."
    models:
      - name: grok-4.6
        label: Grok 4.6
        notes:
          - "Picker description: SpaceXAI's latest frontier model"
        context: 500000
        options:
          - name: Effort
            values:
              - name: Extra High Effort
                notes:
                  - "Extra High Effort - Highest effort and reasoning level"
              - name: High Effort
                notes:
                  - "High Effort - Higher implementation quality with extensive reasoning"
              - name: Medium Effort
                notes:
                  - "Medium Effort - Balanced effort with standard implementation and testing"
              - name: Low Effort
                notes:
                  - "Low Effort - Quick, fast implementations"
      - name: grok-4.5
        label: Grok 4.5
        notes:
          - "The 1.0.34 picker row shows the label alone."
        context: 500000
        options:
          - name: Effort
            values:
              - name: High Effort
                notes:
                  - "High Effort - Highest implementation quality with extensive reasoning"
              - name: Medium Effort
                notes:
                  - "Medium Effort - Balanced effort with standard implementation and testing"
              - name: Low Effort
                notes:
                  - "Low Effort - Quick, fast implementations"

  - cli: Muse
    version: 1.0.3-R2198.1
    last_updated: 2026-09-05
    notes:
      - "First curated Meta Muse entry, added with the provider itself on 2026-09-05."
      - "Model list read 2026-09-05 from muse's own `model/list` reply over the MSP host it serves on stdio (`muse serve`), which is its only enumeration surface - the CLI has no `models` subcommand and `muse exec` cannot list. The reply carried providerId `meta`, profileId `tbh`, and source `providerCatalog`, so the list is account-resolved and complete for this account."
      - "Evidence: docs/research/2026-09-05-meta-muse-cli-probe.md"
      - "`name` is the raw id `muse --model` accepts (the reply's `modelId`); `label` is a rendering of the reply's `displayLabel`, which upstream sets equal to the id."
      - "The `-contributor` rows are the same models on terms Meta describes as \"Your content, including inter-session messages, may be used for product improvement.\" They are listed so an operator can choose one deliberately."
      - "No entry is marked default even though `model/list` flags `muse-spark-1.3-contributor` as `isDefault`. Projecting that here would make every runtime turn opt into content sharing without the operator asking for it; with no `--model` argument muse still uses whatever the account prefers."
      - "`context: 1007997` and `max_output: 128000` are the reply's `contextLimit` and `outputLimit`, identical across all four rows. `cost` is null upstream and is therefore omitted rather than guessed."
      - "The effort menu is provider-wide, not per model: `--reasoning-effort` is a root argument on both `muse` and `muse exec`, and its help states one list for every model - none, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra - with `high` as the default. That is why it sits in shared_options and no model overrides it."
    shared_options:
      - name: Reasoning effort
        values:
          - name: none
            notes:
              - "No reasoning budget."
          - name: minimal
            notes:
              - "Minimal reasoning budget."
          - name: low
            notes:
              - "Quick responses with lighter reasoning."
          - name: medium
            notes:
              - "Balances speed and reasoning depth."
          - name: high
            notes:
              - "Greater reasoning depth for complex problems."
          - name: xhigh
            notes:
              - "Extra high reasoning depth."
          - name: max
            notes:
              - "Maximum reasoning depth."
          - name: ultra
            notes:
              - "Highest reasoning budget muse exposes."
        default: high
    models:
      - name: muse-spark-1.3
        label: muse-spark-1.3
        notes:
          - "releaseDate 2026-09-02; the catalog carries no description for this row."
        context: 1007997
        max_output: 128000
      - name: muse-spark-1.3-contributor
        label: muse-spark-1.3 (contributor)
        notes:
          - "Catalog description: Your content, including inter-session messages, may be used for product improvement."
          - "Marked isDefault by `model/list`; deliberately not marked default here."
        context: 1007997
        max_output: 128000
      - name: muse-spark-1.2
        label: muse-spark-1.2
        notes:
          - "releaseDate 2026-08-05; the catalog carries no description for this row."
        context: 1007997
        max_output: 128000
      - name: muse-spark-1.2-contributor
        label: muse-spark-1.2 (contributor)
        notes:
          - "Catalog description: Your content, including inter-session messages, may be used for product improvement."
        context: 1007997
        max_output: 128000

